 ## Background
-The method originates from the need for real-time volumetric lighting in games, where full Monte Carlo solutions to the radiative transport equation are too slow [S1]. It was popularized by techniques like those in *Crysis* (2007) for screen-space god rays, but evolved into ray marching approaches in engines like Unreal Engine 5 and Unity HDRP to support multiple lights and correct occlusion [S3, unofficial]. The theoretical basis lies in the volume rendering equation, with single-scattering approximations allowing for real-time evaluation by decoupling the in-scattering term from unknown radiance [S1].
